<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:28.060
<b>The Coming of Age Ceremony</b>

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.560
Okay, shoot it!

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.570
And again. Shoot it!

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:36.570
I can't, I still need to swap the dry plate!

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.870
Turn off the radio! I can't concentrate!

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.580
Is this Bostonia Castle?

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.290
This is Hugh Solts' Observatory.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.290
Got it. Continue to observe the situation.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.090
Colonel.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.090
We should hurry and get the parade underway.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.300
Our party crashers will be here before long.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:01:59.970
It stopped!

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.300
Sochie! Congrats on your first solo flight!

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.890
Don't bother with compliments.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.270
Regardless of your flight time, a pass is a pass.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.480
But he still beat me, right?

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.780
Loran just has a special knack for machines.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.280
Well, he only started this because I told him too.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.410
Sochie, even though you're a girl of the Heim family-

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.990
-you still want to be a militia pilot.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.580
You're special as well.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:26.290
'Cause I have a friend like you whose dad builds planes.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.580
I'll leave the inheritance stuff to my sister.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.290
I don't want to end up as the wife of some politician or merchant.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.880
Aren't you choosy.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.380
Do they really have to hold the militia's parade the day before the summer solstice?

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.970
<i>Well, it's already been decided.</i>

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.850
Isn't that the same day as the Coming of Age Ceremony?

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.390
Yeah, it's a shame that I can't attend your guys' ceremony.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.980
I have to fly this in the parade.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.070
Because they chose the plane your dad made, right?

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.900
Alright, we're done.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:04.200
Oh man... Looks like Rhineford hasn't contracted our factory to produce all the planes.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.990
He's producing half of 'em in his own factories.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:10.870
But doesn't mass production require a lot of money?

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.290
They've been making planes here since my grandfather's generation!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.880
And now it's your time to get some profit in return. Nice, isn't it?

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.090
They say surprises are what win wars.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:25.810
If we use these planes in a naval battle, we'll give Gauria's leadership a good scare.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.890
Get that machine gun installed! What the hell are you doing?!

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.600
Why are they holding the parade that day?

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:36.770
If it was after the ceremony, as a militia recruit, I could've been in the parade!

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.400
No! The seat's hot!

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.190
It's not as hot if you sit in the back.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.570
<i>You're not hot, Loran?</i>

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.200
I'm the chauffeur here.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.280
Are you really gonna join the militia?

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.490
Yep.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.290
You should too, Loran. You should join the militia!

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.000
The Master's the one who gets to decide that.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.380
Miashei, you try talking to him!

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.590
Sochie, does your father agree with you doing this?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.590
I can take care of my own business!

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.300
Do your best at the ceremony, alright?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.800
I'm looking forward to the parade.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.970
Thanks!

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.580
Today is my Coming of Age Ceremony!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:45.890
Hold still!

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:46.890
That stings!

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.800
You don't handle pain well at all.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.180
It stings bad!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.390
So you go camping and fall on your butt? That's dumb.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.890
Really?

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:57.270
Today is going to be a busy day. Go get changed.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:57.770
Ma'am.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.570
It's the militia.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.780
They're all going to be in Nocis for the parade.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.370
Loudspeakers and searchlights...

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:16.870
Keep your eyes on the road!

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:17.880
I'm sorry!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.670
Go right! Right!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.500
This is amazing.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.180
It's even bigger than I imagined.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:32.100
Is it really okay for them to hold the militia's parade on the same day as the Coming of Age Ceremony in Vicinity?

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.520
Lord Guin is sure going to have a lot on his plate.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.690
<i>We're so close to Main Street, but it's so quiet.</i>

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.190
<i>That's because we're using this as a dormitory.</i>

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.690
Even so, don't you think it's too big?

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.150
We're too early!

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:54.370
We used your measurements from about a month ago, so it should be a close fit.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.000
Did you lose weight?

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.080
No, I'm still the same.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:01.090
<i>Miss Kihel just keeps looking more and more like Her Majesty Dianna.</i>

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.090
I'm jealous you get to go to the party at Bostonia Castle.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.470
You'll get your chance in a couple of years.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.800
Besides, the ceremony's today!

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.470
How's the university?

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.470
I won't know until I start.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.980
They'll just be teaching me things I already know anyway.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.600
I want to be part of society.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.190
My, what are you saying?!

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.690
Could you talk to them for me, Father?

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.570
I want to work in the castle administration.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.490
You need some pictures on these walls.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.070
Father!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.370
Well, I can probably help negotiate a part time job for you.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.030
I want to be part of society!

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.700
Kihel!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.000
Enough about that!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.450
The parade is about to start!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.790
<i>We have to be in Nocis City by three!</i>

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.880
<i>Do you remember where to the garden's at?</i>

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:43.290
Yes, sir.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.090
Oh? You're not going with them, Loran?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.800
Chauffeurs aren't allowed to sit in the guest seats.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:49.800
Oh.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.680
Are you going to see your friends in Nocis City?

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.890
l don't think I can...

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:55.600
It's no big deal. Today is a special day.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.500
Greet Inglessa's ruler, Lord Rhineford! Salute!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:29.470
Truly an amazing parade, is it not?

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:33.300
Can Gauria's forces really cross the Atlantic and come attack us here?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.890
This is all that's stopping them.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:38.100
That's why we need this kind of organized army.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.680
So you're really gonna join the militia?

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.100
It's just like how you want to have a normal job instead of going to college.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.480
That's bad behavior.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.870
Look! The militia's fighter squadron is coming.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.700
Why do Earth people always look at what's above them, but never at what's below?

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.250
Because they can't get off the ground.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.290
Hey, what are you two gonna do when the Return begins?

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.000
I don't really want to live with the Returners.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.090
I'm gonna keep learning how to bake.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.880
I want to make bread for everyone.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.800
I'm going to become a journalist.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.430
And you?

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:19.180
After the Coming of Age Ceremony today, I'll be a Vicinity citizen.

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.890
<i>It's the Air Force! There's so many...!</i>

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.270
Miashei's in one of those!

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.980
It's the Air Force.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.990
Do you think they'll use those to fight against Dianna Counter?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.700
They're meant to be a counterforce against Gaurian ships.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:40.370
I wonder if Queen Dianna has ever slept on the Earth's surface.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:43.790
Dianna Soriel is coming here for the first time.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.170
What are you gonna do at Vicinity's Coming of Age Ceremony?

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:51.510
No idea. But hey, isn't the mystery half the fun of it?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.470
If you think about it that way, I guess so.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.090
A cannon salute?

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.100
Fire!

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.990
<i>In any case, your assistance would be appreciated.</i>

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.490
I'll help you out. Please rest assured.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.540
Excuse me.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.670
<i>Laura. Laura!</i>

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.010
Are you looking for Mister Heim?

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:33.960
Yes, sir.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.050
Get me Mister Diran Heim!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.590
After the ceremony's over with, how would you like to work at Bostonia Castle?

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.470
U-uh... Nocis City is too urban for my liking.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.270
I think Vicinity suits me better.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:48.100
In that case, I'd like you to work for Sid.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.770
These days, a miner like him needs the help of a technician as well.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.480
Mr. Sid, you say?

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.570
You know him, don't you?

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.570
Yes.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.860
If this is about a job, would you consider hiring me for it?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.280
Well, well...

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.870
I have no interest in going to college to learn useless theories.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:06.000
In this era, I'd rather learn practical things and contribute as a member of society.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.660
Indeed.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:12.170
Heir, please excuse me and my two daughters for having to leave early.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.800
I'm terribly sorry.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.800
My elder daughter and I will be attending the party tonight.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.680
Feel free, the ceremony is more important anyway.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:24.100
Laura, take some time to consider working for Sid.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:24.430
Yes, sir.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:28.980
Excuse me.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:35.690
Lord Guin, why do you keep calling Loran, "Laura"?

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:37.400
Oh, that...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.070
I simply think Laura suits him better.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.080
Laura, do you think you can work for Sid?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.580
I'm not Laura. I'm Loran.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.290
But Lord Guin always says, "Laura, Laura, Laura!"

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.090
They go here and here, right?

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.590
There are six spots altogether.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:57.880
They're all above the waist.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:10:59.880
Around here?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.090
That tickles!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:03.720
Six spots...

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.180
I wonder if I'll find someone drowning again?

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:14.770
The ceremony is essentially about doing whatever you like before the White Doll for the night.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:19.400
Well, the most important part is the Holy Carving Ceremony.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.700
Right. The Holy Carving Ceremony?

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.280
- Let me see your back.
- Sir.

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.370
Here, here, and here.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.700
You'll be carving the marks on these six spots.

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.080
Why?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.580
Because the Priest who speaks of the White Doll also has those marks.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.590
But why are the marks there?

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.970
It's an old legend, so it can't be helped.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.680
Do I press my finger on those spots to make the marks?

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.600
That's not gonna do it.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.890
That's all the men need to know.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:50.390
You just need to concentrate on the girl.

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:07.200
One, two!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.790
Now, do it! Raise it up!

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.580
To Mountain Cycle!

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.970
If only my wife were here right now...

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:42.900
Hey.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.780
Good evening.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.780
You told me today that you wanted to witness the new era, no?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.790
I'd be happy just to dance.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:54.370
I'll show you some things from the new era later.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:03.380
And now, as the one chosen to stand before the White Doll, I shall now begin...

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.890
...the Holy carving ceremony. Who wishes to go up with me?

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.770
Me! Pick me!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.600
- That Tom! 
 - What a freak!

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:18.110
- Go for it!
- Don't lose to the others!

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.570
The Earth is great!

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:29.570
Everyone, hurry up and come here!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.370
Loran Cehack!

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:37.290
Are these the machines that can communicate without any wires?

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:38.880
Yes.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.000
We receive signals from the Moonrace with them.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.380
You mean there's a race of people living on the moon?

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:48.390
I've organized the militia because they plan on immigrating here.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.180
There are that many people coming here?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.100
Not just to Inglessa.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:56.890
They want me to hand over most of North Ameria and the Sunbelt Zone.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:14:00.560
Those are the demands of the spacenoids living on the moon.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.280
I had no idea you were working this hard.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.580
Where is it!?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.880
Any reports from the militia?!

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:27.380
<i>Sir! All troops are now on patrol!</i>

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:30.800
Report!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.970
<i>We've got nothing!</i>

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.400
Why the hell do they want the militia to fly at night?!

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:43.770
You're not officially a member of the militia yet!

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:47.490
I've logged plenty of fight time in that Hipheavy you made, dad!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:54.700
What do you think of this, Sid?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:58.370
In an age where planes are flying in the sky, they're still holding a ceremony like this.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.370
Human behavior doesn't always end up being logical.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.290
Makes no difference to me.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.590
If anything, the ceremony prevents others from coming up the mountain,

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:07.960
which makes this the best time for us to investigate.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:15.970
Ready, Loran?

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.890
I-I don't know what to do. How do I do this?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.770
Turn around and take off your clothes, Loran.

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:26.980
M-ma'am!

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.700
Then give me the six holy marks.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:31.910
The holy marks...

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.780
The way you learned earlier.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.280
I-I know.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.370
Hurry up!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.370
R-right!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.290
Jeez, this is so embarrassing.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:47.590
I don't believe you! You can't bring a toy like that to the Coming of Age Ceremony!

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.670
Really? But this is the last night I'll...

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.550
T-these are...

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.180
W-w-what the heck are these?!

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.260
Leeches, obviously.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.770
That's what you carve the marks on my back with.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:00.980
They're coming out...

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:03.190
Just hurry up and put them on my back!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.270
B-but...

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.060
<i>I'll put them on you after this.</i>

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:07.070
Come on out...

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:09.570
- They're leeches!
- I don't believe it!
- That's how it's always been!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.940
- You knew that, right?!
- Eww!

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:16.200
I-if I don't do this, you won't become an adult...

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.370
You've waited two years for this!

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:22.500
You know where they go, right?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.790
Y-yeah.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.290
What are you doing?!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.290
The White Doll is watching us!

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.670
Now I wonder if you're actually capable of becoming a man by completing this ceremony for the rest of the night!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.590
Don't you want to be recognized as an adult?

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.270
Again...?

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.060
What?

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:50.480
I saw a flash coming from Nocis City.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.780
<i>It's the color of fire!</i>

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:52.900
<i>It really is a fire!</i>

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.070
Hey, Loran! Can you see where it is!?

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:57.200
It's definitely coming from Nocis!

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.080
It's a huge fire!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.490
It looks like the whole city is burning.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.670
What the...? Searchlights?

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:08.790
Is it a bombing?

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.100
What the... Are they serious?!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.100
What annoying pests!

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.600
Benjam!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.980
Benjam, head back and take Nocis City.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:31.400
I'll head west and hold our position.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.490
<i>But the militia is attacking!</i>

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:36.200
Why the hell are you worried about the militia's pathetic firepower?!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.490
<i>Terribly sorry, ma'am!</i>

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:38.200
Then go back!

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.170
What the heck is that?!

00:17:58.470 --> 00:17:59.680
They're serious?!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.680
It's running!

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.390
But it looks like it's a machine!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.180
The Bull-Ones are firing!

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.690
Barbarians...

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.980
Don't toy with me!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:35.300
<i>It's a long-range beam. Warship level...</i>

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:38.090
<i>The ones I saw being used in Dianna Counter's training sessions.</i>

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.680
Loran, we need to carry out the ceremony throughout the rest of the night!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:41.720
B-but...

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:50.770
- What!?
 - What the?!

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:55.690
Loran!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.410
Sochie and Loran are being buried alive!

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.970
This is...

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.600
What is this? What the heck just happened!?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:24.890
l don't know.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.390
The White Doll crumbled all around us.

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:29.770
What's that!?

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.480
<i>The cockpit is...!</i>

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.900
It's moving! Something lit up!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.690
What the heck is it?

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.070
It's a cockpit!

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.280
What's a "cockpit"?

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:42.570
It's a driver's seat. You've never heard of it?

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.570
That's the seat.

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:46.080
What are you doing?

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.080
I'm getting in.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.790
Can something like this actually move?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.080
It's the White Doll!

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.080
But those lights are flashing.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:53.630
Doesn't it look like it can move?

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.590
This is definitely a driver's seat.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.800
It moved!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:19:59.800
<i>Sochie!</i>

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.470
It looks like the head's moving!

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.090
It's safer in here.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:04.890
Please step down!

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:07.100
Now how do I get this thing to move?

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.390
How am I supposed to know?!

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:11.680
It's got an MET interface...

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:13.480
The control panel's totally different.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:20.900
Ow...

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:21.900
I just touched this, and--

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:22.780
We're moving!

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:23.910
No way!

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:36.170
It looks like the arm's moving!

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.090
It's a beam rifle!

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.800
There was a mechanical doll inside the White Doll?

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.890
It looks like there was.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.100
<i>This is a mobile suit!</i>

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.270
<i>How did a mobile suit become part of an ancient ruin?</i>

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.190
Sochie, get down!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.870
I'm detecting a mobile suit?!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:09.280
There shouldn't be any mobile suits here on Earth!

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:12.790
It fired!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:20.590
They're going for the city! Why?!

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:22.800
It's moving on its own. I can't stop it!

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.380
- Make it stop!
- How?!

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:31.260
I got hit?! Damage report!

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.600
The next shot could be a direct hit!

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:51.200
Why didn't Dianna Counter report any Intel about this?!

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:05.300
It stopped.

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:09.680
B-but... the lights in the driver's seat haven't gone out yet.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:11.100
Then can it still move?

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:12.600
I'll try to see if I can make it move.

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:14.600
It's burning! The city is burning!

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:15.350
Where?!

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:44.190
<i>I don't want Miss Kihel and Milady Sochie to get involved in this war.</i>

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:47.480
<i>But Nocis City seems to have taken a lot of damage...</i>

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:49.280
<i>Even the Master and his house were...</i>

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:56.520
<i>Keith wants to get away from it all. I end up going to the White Doll, even though I don't know why.</i>

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:00.710
<i>Next time, on  </i>Turn A Gundam:<i></i>

00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:02.370
<i>After the Ceremony.</i>

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:04.630
"The winds of war are blowing."

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>After the Ceremony</b>
